The module below should export `createRouteTable(routes)`. `routes` must be an array of descriptors `{ method, path, handler }`. `method` must be a non-empty uppercase string. `path` must be `'*'` or begin with `/`. A descriptor must own a `handler` property, whose value may be anything. Malformed arrays or descriptors throw `TypeError`.

The function must snapshot each descriptor into a new internal record without mutating the input and return `{ resolve }`. `resolve(method, path)` applies the same method validation, requires a path beginning with `/`, and returns a handler. An exact method-and-path match always takes priority over wildcard-path routes, regardless of input order. Among multiple exact matches, use the first; otherwise use the first wildcard with the same method. Return `null` when nothing matches. Empty route arrays are valid.

The implementation has one bug. Return a corrected complete CommonJS source file exporting `createRouteTable` directly.

```javascript
'use strict';

function validMethod(method) {
  return typeof method === 'string' && method.length > 0 && method === method.toUpperCase();
}

function createRouteTable(routes) {
  if (!Array.isArray(routes)) throw new TypeError('routes must be an array');
  const snapshot = routes.map((route) => {
    if (!route || typeof route !== 'object' || Array.isArray(route) ||
        !validMethod(route.method) ||
        (route.path !== '*' && (typeof route.path !== 'string' || !route.path.startsWith('/'))) ||
        !Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(route, 'handler')) {
      throw new TypeError('Invalid route');
    }
    return { method: route.method, path: route.path, handler: route.handler };
  });

  function resolve(method, path) {
    if (!validMethod(method) || typeof path !== 'string' || !path.startsWith('/')) {
      throw new TypeError('Invalid lookup');
    }
    const match = snapshot.find((route) =>
      route.method === method && (route.path === path || route.path === '*')
    );
    return match ? match.handler : null;
  }

  return { resolve };
}

module.exports = createRouteTable;
```

